  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOM-Engagement Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Engagement Facility is designed as a simplified, flexible, and rapid response mechanism to support upstream policy initiatives and innovation within UNDP&#x2019;s programming framework. It combines the functions of Development Support Services (DSS) and Development Advisory Services (DAS) to facilitate time-sensitive advisory services, knowledge product development, and testing innovations for scaling. This facility aims to streamline procedures, reduce transaction costs, and enhance the UNDPs ability to respond to emerging policy needs effectively, contributing to results in the Country Programme Document (CPD) and government-requested activities. Key features include direct resource allocation, demand-driven activity funding, and integration into UNDPs Programme and Project Management framework. Results and activities are monitored and reported through the ROAR system.</narrative>
  </description>
